{
  "id": "ep078",
  "duration": 50.384,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 3.587,
      "text": "Our universe could vanish in an instant with zero warning.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Illustration of an Isolated Black Hole (52675793824).png",
        "credit": "NASA Hubble",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Illustration_of_an_Isolated_Black_Hole_(52675793824).png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.6,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.587,
      "end": 9.957,
      "text": "It's called false vacuum decay, where a sudden shift in cosmic energy destroys space itself.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Illustration of an Isolated Black Hole (52675793824).png",
        "credit": "NASA Hubble",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Illustration_of_an_Isolated_Black_Hole_(52675793824).png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.6,
          "end": 9.967,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 9.957,
      "end": 17.777,
      "text": "Physicist Sidney Coleman established the mathematical framework for this catastrophic process in 1977.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 9.967,
          "end": 17.767,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 17.777,
      "end": 23.297,
      "text": "Calculations show our entire universe exists in this fragile, temporary state.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "CERN OpenDays @ LHC 02.jpg",
        "credit": "SimonWaldherr",
        "license": "CC BY 4.0",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CERN_OpenDays_@_LHC_02.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 17.767,
          "end": 23.3,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 23.297,
      "end": 28.117,
      "text": "Fortunately, this collapse is estimated to not happen for trillions of years.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "HubbleDeepField.800px.jpg",
        "credit": "Robert Williams (NASA, ESA, STScI)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HubbleDeepField.800px.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 23.3,
          "end": 26.6,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 26.6,
          "end": 28.133,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 28.117,
      "end": 34.242,
      "text": "Yet, researchers recently simulated these destructive bubbles using a quantum computer.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Quantum Computing; Ion Trapping (5941055642).jpg",
        "credit": "National Institute of Standards and Technology",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Quantum_Computing;_Ion_Trapping_(5941055642).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 28.133,
          "end": 32.4,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 32.4,
          "end": 34.233,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 34.242,
      "end": 42.787,
      "text": "Using a 5,564-qubit D-Wave processor, they found a true vacuum bubble expands at the speed of light.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 34.233,
          "end": 42.8,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 42.787,
      "end": 50.034,
      "text": "These findings, published in Nature Physics in 2025, prove a cosmic erasure would strike with zero warning.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Illustration of an Isolated Black Hole (52675793824).png",
        "credit": "NASA Hubble",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Illustration_of_an_Isolated_Black_Hole_(52675793824).png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 42.8,
          "end": 50.4,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
